# Electric smooth nose profile — 2026-10-25

The owner's side-view screenshot identifies an unwanted S-shaped hood/nose transition. Subsequent front and overhead screenshots request an inward taper and expose dented shading. ENP01–ENP04 address all three corrections: a continuous nose profile, a bonnet that narrows toward the front, and coherent reflections across its fitted border. Matched blue/white views reproduce the supplied viewing directions for both detail levels.

| Requirement | Implementation and actual evidence |
| --- | --- |
| ENP01: remove the S bend | A monotonic cubic hood section replaces the sinusoidal center depression and localized nose correction. The side shoulder uses a convex quadratic section. One convex bumper profile replaces the sum of a low parabola and separate upper roll. |
| ENP02: make the transition smooth | Hood control tangents follow fixed-X nose sections, including the changing body width. Lid, surround and nose share transverse sampling stations. The simpler model retains those transverse samples to avoid a reverse facet. Actual plane sections at X=0, 0.40 and 0.65 m cover hood, brow and bumper. |
| ENP03: taper the bonnet toward the nose | The fitted panel narrows in plan toward the light brow. Actual prepared-mesh rows near its front/rear measure about 1.330/1.546 m full, a ratio of 0.860; the simpler model also measures 0.860. Existing outer body and tyre clearance remain. |
| ENP04: remove the damaged appearance | Lid and border normals come from one master surface, evaluated at a stable scale. Differentiating the narrow border's own parameterization had produced badly inconsistent normals. The isolated old-normal calculation on identical geometry gives seam p95 angles of 75.80°/78.69°; the correction gives 1.846° in both detail levels. New actual-normal bounds reject the old calculation. |
| V01: demonstrate the correction | Equal 20 mm arcs of the actual baked mesh give a maximum reverse turn of about 0.285° full / 0.283° simple, below the unchanged 1° bound. The exact original model measures up to 6.384° / 7.154° and fails twelve of the final 32 checks. Matching side, head-on and high-angle captures are in the [gallery](evidence/electric-smooth-nose-2026-10-25/gallery.html). |
| R01: retain accepted behavior and construction | Exact task-start hashes retain model assembly, `car_visual.gd`, the original model suite and the body-finish suite. Concurrent owner-authorized physics 0.71 / electric-9 changes are preserved, recorded with before/current hashes and excluded from this geometry checkpoint. Their final hashes match the [launch-drift report](evidence/electric-launch-drift-2026-10-25/report.json). Existing gap depth, seam equality, symmetry, rear recess, finite-normal and triangle-budget assertions remain. This task edits no production camera, input or canonical physics source. |
| G01 / Q01: refresh and checkpoint | Catalogue art, all 49 appearance photos and the news image are regenerated and imported. Exact baselines, command logs, metrics and a task-only binary Git checkpoint accompany the [report](evidence/electric-smooth-nose-2026-10-25/report.json). |

The runtime edit is confined to `game/vehicle/electric_coachwork.gd`. Prepared v7 contains **537** resources: **362 exact original binaries** and 175 changed resources. Serialized-byte comparison ignores only Godot's random local ArrayMesh IDs before reusing exact originals. V6 is verified against its exact backup before retiring from the game export. Full/simple triangle counts are **169,734 / 70,506**, inside the existing 170,000 cap. The simpler model adds 4,340 triangles relative to the preceding model to retain the nose silhouette and fitted border; these counts are not physical-device performance measurements.

Two prior shape expectations are superseded by this explicit owner correction. `test_electric_hood.gd` replaces the required 15–70 mm raised-shoulder depression with a restrained transverse crown of less than 25 mm. `test_electric_rounded_front.gd` replaces the required lower bumper protrusion with the corrected light-brow-leading relationship. Its transverse roundness and lower-edge tuck bounds remain. The new strict curvature gate tests the owner's requested smooth profile on real prepared meshes; baseline failures are retained. No seam, depth, symmetry, normal, budget, physics or input tolerance is relaxed.

Initial off-center sections exposed folded front strips caused by incompatible lid/surround transverse parameterization; matching their stations fixes that geometry. A tangent taken at constant normalized width then left an off-center kink; using fixed-X nose tangents corrects it. Individual triangle intersections produce sub-millimetre angular noise, so the curvature fixture samples equal 20 mm arc lengths while retaining the 1° reverse-turn threshold. The simpler model still failed at 1.208°; retaining its front transverse subdivisions corrects that failure. Initial logs and measurements remain in the evidence folder.

The later taper prototype exposed the narrow-strip normal defect in the owner's overhead view. `hood_normal()` differentiates the master hood parameterization instead, and the optional per-UV normal callback applies the same frame to lid and surround. An isolated `--local-normals` test disables only that callback in process memory and rebuilds the same geometry; it retains 32 checks / 2 expected normal failures plus matching images. The new seam test compares actual neighbouring mesh normals and retains p95 <3° / maximum <15° bounds. No shipping file is changed by this diagnostic. An initial concurrent `TrackBrowser` parse interruption during import is retained; a normal sequential retry passes without editing that work.

Pinned Godot 4.7.2 runs through `scripts/dev.ps1`; [run_validation.ps1](evidence/electric-smooth-nose-2026-10-25/run_validation.ps1) records all final commands and actual outcomes. Model, curvature, hood, retained roundness, body joins, native App Garage/race, electric driving, one-pedal, art/import and parser results are collected in the report. The geometry tests include full/simple production meshes; both Compatibility and desktop Mobile have native captures.

